1. WHAT IS ORM?

Answer:

    ORM = Object Relational Mapping

Mapping:

    Java Class      → Database Table
    Java Object     → Table Row
    Java Field      → Column
    Relationship    → Foreign Key

Example:

    @Entity
    public class Account {

        @Id
        private Long id;

        private String accountNumber;
    }

When To Use:

    Use ORM when working with relational databases
    using Java objects instead of JDBC.

───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

2. WHAT IS JPA?

Answer:

    JPA (Jakarta Persistence API)
    is a specification.

Defines:

    • @Entity
    • @Table
    • @Id
    • EntityManager
    • Query APIs

Important:

    JPA Defines Rules

    Hibernate Implements Rules

───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

3. WHAT IS HIBERNATE?

Answer:

    Hibernate is an ORM Framework
    and JPA Implementation.

Features:

    • ORM
    • SQL Generation
    • Lazy Loading
    • Dirty Checking
    • Caching
    • HQL
    • Batch Processing

───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

4. WHAT IS SPRING DATA JPA?

Answer:

    Repository layer built over JPA.

Example:

    public interface AccountRepository
           extends JpaRepository<
               Account,
               Long> {
    }

Built-in Methods:

    save()
    findById()
    findAll()
    deleteById()
    count()

Benefits:

    • Less Boilerplate
    • Easy CRUD
    • Pagination
    • Sorting

───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

5. JPA vs HIBERNATE vs SPRING DATA JPA

JPA

    Specification

Hibernate

    ORM & JPA Provider

Spring Data JPA

    Repository Abstraction

Interview Answer:

    JPA → Defines

    Hibernate → Implements

    Spring Data JPA → Simplifies

